    "description": "Four Claude Code shortcuts from the docs: Shift+Tab cycles permission modes (Alt+M on Windows without VT input mode), Ctrl+R searches your history, Ctrl+V pastes an image (Alt+V on Windows and WSL), and Esc twice on an empty prompt opens the rewind menu.",
    "companion_text": "Follow Promptwerk for more Claude workflows, step by step. Based on the Interactive mode and Keybindings pages of the Claude Code docs; the terminal scene is an animated view, not a screen recording. Per the docs, shortcuts may vary by platform and terminal. Shift+Tab cycles through default (shown as Manual), acceptEdits and plan, and when available bypassPermissions and auto. If the prompt already has text, Esc twice clears it instead; press Up to get the draft back. In iTerm2 on macOS, paste images with Cmd+V. Set your own shortcuts with /keybindings in ~/.claude/keybindings.json.",
